---
import PageSite from "@layouts/PageSite.astro";
import PageHead from "@components/redesign/PageHead.astro";
---

<PageSite title="Departments" description="What each of StuyPulse's four departments does: Mechanical Engineering, Software Engineering, Business and Strategy." fullBleed>
  <PageHead title="Departments" intro="Everyone on StuyPulse joins one of four departments. Here's what each one does.">
    <div class="actions"><a class="pill pill-white" href="/join">How to join</a></div>
  </PageHead>

  <div class="band depts">
    <section id="mechanical" aria-labelledby="mech">
      <span class="ic"><img src="/icons/mechanical.svg" alt="" /></span>
      <div>
        <h2 id="mech">Mechanical Engineering</h2>
        <p>
          Mechanical Engineering designs and builds the robot. Every build season the department splits into groups of 4 to 6
          students, each with at least one veteran member. Each group focuses on one part of the robot, such as the drive train,
          electronics or a mechanism. Sometimes two mechanism groups compete for the better design.
        </p>
        <p>
          The President and Vice President of Mechanical Engineering keep the groups running smoothly, with directors for
          machining, lab safety, procurement, electronics, design, field construction and more. See who they are on the
          <a href="/about/leadership#mechanical">leadership page</a>.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section id="software" aria-labelledby="soft">
      <span class="ic"><img src="/icons/software.svg" alt="" /></span>
      <div>
        <h2 id="soft">Software Engineering</h2>
        <p>
          Software writes the code that controls the robot on the field and keeps its electronics running. They also keep every
          old robot's code working, so the robots are ready for demos.
        </p>
        <p>
          Most new members have little or no programming experience, so we teach everyone Java from the start. It's no easy
          task in a short season, but it pays off when our code drives a 120 lb robot across the field. All of our code, past
          and present, is open source on <a href="https://github.com/StuyPulse">GitHub</a>. Some files may carry a different
          license, so check each file's comments.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section id="business" aria-labelledby="biz">
      <span class="ic"><img src="/icons/business.svg" alt="" /></span>
      <div>
        <h2 id="biz">Business</h2>
        <p>
          Business handles everything that keeps the team running: fundraising, sponsors, branding, meals during build season,
          travel, award submissions and outreach. The President and Vice President of Business are the main contact for our
          sponsors.
        </p>
        <p>
          The Director of Public Relations coordinates outreach, including mentoring FLL, FTC and FRC teams and running our
          social media. The Director of Finance keeps the budget stable and works with sponsors.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section id="strategy" aria-labelledby="strat">
      <span class="ic"><img src="/icons/strategy.svg" alt="" /></span>
      <div>
        <h2 id="strat">Strategy</h2>
        <p>
          Strategy helps decide how the robot should be designed, how it plays each match, and which teams we pick as
          alliance partners.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>
  </div>
</PageSite>

<style>
  .depts {
    max-width: 1120px;
    display: grid;
    gap: 64px;
  }
  section {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 96px 1fr;
    gap: clamp(20px, 4vw, 44px);
    scroll-margin-top: 16px;
  }
  .ic {
    display: grid;
    place-items: center;
    width: 96px;
    height: 96px;
    border-radius: 50%;
    background: var(--blush);
  }
  .ic img {
    width: 48px;
  }
  h2 {
    font-size: clamp(2rem, 3.6vw, 3rem);
    margin: 18px 0 0;
  }
  p {
    margin: 16px 0 0;
    max-width: 68ch;
    font-size: 18px;
  }
  p a {
    text-decoration: underline;
    text-underline-offset: 3px;
  }
  @media (max-width: 640px) {
    section {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }
    .ic {
      width: 72px;
      height: 72px;
    }
    .ic img {
      width: 36px;
    }
  }
</style>
